  "english": "THE SEVEN-DAY CYCLES OF THE ROMANS 4.\n\nIn January:\n\n6. Tuesday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ our God. The intervening period of eating is forty-one days.\n\n14. Wednesday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. Fast. Penitential Father [Harts] Tone 1 [A-dz - A / First Class]: \"The youths sang in the furnace and said\" (Yergeyin mankunkn i hnocin yev asyein).\n\n15. Thursday. Tone 3 [GD - G / Third Class]. Feast of the Birth of John the Forerunner [Precursor].\n\n17. Saturday. Tone 4 [D-dz - D / Fourth Class]. [Feast of] Peter the Patriarch, Blaise the Bishop, and Abisalom the Deacon.\n\n18. Sunday. Tone 4 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. First [Sunday]. Hambartsi Tone 4 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]: \"Glory to Your resurrection, O Lord\" (P'ark' harut'yan k'o ter); \"Having taken upon Yourself the cross\" (Khach'il i yandzn) to the end.\n\n19. Monday. Tone 1 [AD - A / First Class]. [Feast of] Anton the Anchorite.\n\n20. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AK - A-flat / First Side]. [Feast of] Theodosius the King and the Holy Babes of Ephesus.\n\n21. Wednesday. Tone 2 [BD - B / Second Class]. Penitential Father [Harts] Tone 1 [AK - A-flat / First Side]: \"Glorified forever is the God of our fathers\" (P'aravoryal havytyan astvats harts'n merots').\n\n22. Thursday. Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]. [Feast of] Cyriacus and his mother Julitta, and of the witnesses Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Gregory. Father [Harts] Tone 1 [A-dz - A / First Class]: \"You, the righteous and upright judge\" (Uzk'ez ardar yev ughigh da...).\n\n24. Saturday. Tone 3 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]. [Feast of] Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril, and Gregory the Theologian.\n\n25. Sunday. Tone 4 [DD - D / Fourth Class]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [BK - B-flat / Second Side]: \"By Your voluntary will You came to suffering\" (Kamavorut'yamb yekir i ch'arch'arans). Hambartsi Tone 4 [DD - D / Fourth Class]: \"The archangel [announced] the resurrection of the Son of God\" (Zyarut'yun astvatsordvoyn hreshtakapetn).\n\n26. Monday. Tone 4 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the Virgin, and her father Philip, and her mother Claudia, and the two brothers Sergius and Apiton, and the two eunuchs Protus and Hyacinthus. Father [Harts] Tone 1 [AK - A-flat / First Side]: \"Holy God, Creator of eternity\" (Surb astvats ararich' yavityenits').\n\n27. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AD - A / First Class]. [Feast of] Tryphon, Barsamas, and Onuphrius the Anchorites.\n\n28. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AK - A-flat / First Side]. Penitential Father [Harts] Tone 2 [B-dz - B / Second Class]: \"Who saved the three youths from the furnace\" (Vor abrets'uts'er zeris mankunsn i hnoc'inn).\n\n29. Thursday. Tone 2 [BD - B / Second Class]. [Feast of] Eugenius, Macarius, Valerius, Candidus, and Aquilas. Father [Harts] Tone 1 [AK - A-flat / First Side]: \"Who are exalted and rest in the saints\" (Vor bardzryald es yev i surbs hanguts'yal).\n\n31. Saturday. Tone 3 [GD - G / Third Class]. [Feast of] Thaddeus the Apostle and Sandukht the Virgin. For the Apostle Thaddeus, start from the order set down below in the First Volume after Vardavar; but the Father [Harts] hymns and the tones are to be taken here.\n\nIn February:\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 3 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]. Third [Sunday]. Father [Harts] Tone 3 [GD - G / Third Class]: \"Creator of all creation, O Christ, today\" (Ararich'd araradsots' K'ristos aysor). Hambartsi Tone 3 [GK - G-flat / Third Side]: \"The sight of the lightning-like angel on the stone\" (Tesil p'aylaknadzev zvart'noyn i vimin).\n\n2. Monday. Tone 4 [DD - D / Fourth Class]. [Feast of] Cyprian the Bishop and the forty-five martyrs, and of the virgins Justina, Euphemia, and Christina. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [BD - B / Second Class]: \"You who do not harbor resentment and are most merciful, do not scatter us\" (Anokhakal yev baregut' mi ts'rer).\n\n3. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DK - D-flat / Fourth Side]. [Feast of] Athenogenes the Bishop, and his ten disciples, and the five martyrs. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [BD - B / Second Class]: \"With Your saints we praise You\" (Und surbs k'o barebanemk' uzk'ez).",
